{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/937273-beast-mythos-of-ancient-greece","id":937273,"title":"Beast mythos of Ancient Greece","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-25T14:04:22-07:00","id":937273,"title":"Beast mythos of Ancient Greece","content":"With Dark Eras out, I took some note on the Exarch names of Ancient Greek myth and noted how familiar names to Beast mythos came up, such as Echidna and also the lone hag exarch having one title as Marduk, which was name dropped as the potential Hero who may have defeated the Dark Mother...<br /> <br /> This interested me so here are some of my thoughts in regards to other Ancient Greek mythos we've learned and some fanon that was in my mind before now, mainly putting her for discussion and debate and to see what people may think.<br /> <br /> Originally, I held the belief of the story of the Dark Mother vs. Marduk that the latter Hero could have been a manifestation of the God-Machine, due to the polar opposition Beasts seem to have with the Demons and god-machine stuff in relation to the more natural Gaia-styled Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> So, I was quite fanboying to see the name mentioned under what seemed to be a title of what we knew as Gate, the lone Abyss Exarch (also noted to be the first human or mage in Dark Eras, with Pandora being another name for them @_@). I saw how many of the female Exarch names given from Ancient Greek mages were alternate names from Beast myth as names of the Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> As a side-note, I was interested to see Greek Mages refer to the Abyss as Tartarus, which is also the classical name for the Dark Domains of the Underworld in the Geist corebook (with Erebus being the Autochthonous Depths).<br /> <br /> I was fairly happy to see some confirmation to my opinion that the Titanomachy and rise of the Olympians (Exarchs) in my old Geist's krewe mythos seemed to be the case here.<br /> <br /> The main question I'd like to leave though is more of a discussion on how Ancient Greek Beasts would define their mythos though, rather than the mages and sin-eaters. Marduk is possibly the Abyss Exarch and a name of the Hero of legend that took down the Dark Mother... This also opens doors for kinships of other Ancient Greek splats as mentioned above with this...<br /> <br /> What are your opinions in this matter? How would you play Beasts steeped in Ancient Greece's mythology as Dark Eras and other books paint things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T14:17:53-07:00","id":937285,"title":"","content":"(As a brief aside; Marduk is Babylonian, not Greek.)<br /> <br /> Beasts in Ancient Greece is an idea that's come up a couple of times on these forums; I know someone proposed a Bronze Age Collapse era for Beast where they roam the dying empires as the Sea Peoples ravage everything. Beasts are a natural fit for a mythical Greece, as Echidna slots nicely into the Dark Mother role and they map easily to the role of the Furies (as monstrous enactors of punishment) and as the ostracized creatures like Medusa and Arachne. Ideally, I'd like to see a Beast/Deviant crossiver setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}